%description:

The residual loss rate HARQ leaves for RLC is an exactly known number, and
nothing checks it.

IdealChannelModel decides reception by a coin flip whose probability is
per * harqReduction^(n-1) for the n-th attempt (IdealChannelModel.cc:37). With
harqReduction = 1 the attempts of a MAC PDU are independent and identically
distributed, so the PDU is discarded only when all maxHarqRtx+1 of them fail,
with probability perDl^(maxHarqRtx+1). IdealChannelModel.ned:32 states this
contract in prose, and simulations/nr/rlc/omnetpp.ini:15 states it again as
the reason those scenarios exist; neither is tested.

This grades it over a 3x3 sweep of the base and the exponent, so an error in
either is caught separately, and it does so through the whole
PHY -> MAC -> HARQ -> RLC chain rather than by calling one function: the
scenario is an ordinary cellular downlink, and what is measured is what the
MAC reports having given up on.

Each point carries two further checks. The per-attempt error rate has to equal
perDl, or the residual figure means nothing -- that one is a tripwire, and it
fails first and explains itself if harqReduction stops being neutral. And
because RLC UM does not retransmit, the SDUs the application never receives
have to be the same packets the MAC discarded, which is what makes this an
assertion about the chain rather than about one statistic.

%extraargs: -c HarqResidualLoss

%file: demo.xml
<config>
    <interface among='eNB* eNodeB* enb* *Enb* gNB* gNodeB* gnb* *Gnb* upf* *Upf* mecHost* pgw*' address='10.x.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
    <interface hosts='*' address='192.168.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
</config>

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[Config HarqResidualLoss]
network = simu5g.simulations.nr.networks.SingleCell_Standalone
sim-time-limit = 40s
**.routingRecorder.enabled = false
cmdenv-express-mode = true
cmdenv-status-frequency = 10000000s

output-scalar-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.sca
output-vector-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.vec
**.vector-recording = false

# The counts are what turn a ratio into a graded claim: the tolerance of each
# check is the binomial standard error over its own sample size. Recording them
# here rather than in the shipped NED keeps this test out of every fingerprint.
**.macPacketLossDl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,sum
**.harqErrorRateDl.result-recording-modes = mean,count
# Exact SDU counts at both ends. cbrFrameLoss would be the obvious statistic to
# use instead, but it is computed against CbrSender's declared frame count,
# which is one short of the number it actually sends (CbrSender.cc:53 divides
# the interval by the period and the sender fires at both ends of it), so a
# check built on it would have to tolerate that off-by-one rather than catch it.
**.cbrGeneratedBytes.result-recording-modes = mean,count
**.cbrReceivedBytes.result-recording-modes = mean,count

############### The quantity under test ##############
# The base and the exponent of perDl^(maxHarqRtx+1), swept independently.
# The bases are high enough that even the rarest residual, 0.5^4, is graded
# from a few hundred discards, which is what keeps the runs short.
**.perDl = ${perDl = 0.5, 0.6, 0.7}
**.maxHarqRtx = ${maxHarqRtx = 1, 2, 3}

############### Geometry: one stationary UE, one gNB ##############
*.gnb.mobility.initialX = 450m
*.gnb.mobility.initialY = 300m
*.numUe = 1
*.ue[0].servingNodeId = 0
*.ue[0].nrServingNodeId = 1
*.ue[0].mobility.initialX = 450m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialY = 350m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinX = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinY = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinZ = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxX = 1000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxY = 1000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxZ = 0m
**.mobility.initFromDisplayString = false

############### Channel: a configurable error rate, nothing else ##############
# No propagation at all, so the loss rate is the configured number rather than
# an emergent property of geometry and MCS selection.
*.gnb.cellularNic.channelModelType = "IdealChannelModel"
*.ue[*].cellularNic.nrChannelModelType = "IdealChannelModel"

# Independent attempts. This is the assumption the closed form rests on.
**.harqReduction = 1

# A clean uplink, so nothing on the feedback path is confounded with the
# downlink losses under test.
**.perUl = 0
**.perD2D = 0

# Keep the loss process off the traffic source's stream, so that changing the
# error rate does not change which SDUs are offered.
num-rngs = 2
**.channelModel[*].rng-0 = 1
**.nrChannelModel[*].rng-0 = 1

############### RLC UM: losses are not repaired ##############
# UM has no ARQ, so a discarded MAC PDU is an SDU the application never sees.
*.bearerConfigurator.onDemandDrbs = [{coreNetwork: "5gc", isDefault: true, suppressSdapHeader: true, lcg: 3, rlcMode: "UM"}]

############### Deterministic CBR traffic, downlink ##############
# 100 SDU/s over 34s is about 3400 HARQ processes per point. That is what
# sets how tight the tolerances can be; it is also well under the one-PDU-per-
# TTI ceiling, so the link never saturates and the only losses are the coin
# flips. Raising the rate to the point of saturation adds queueing loss on top
# and destroys the measurement.
*.ue[*].numApps = 1
*.server.numApps = 1
*.ue[*].app[0].typename = "CbrReceiver"
*.ue[*].app[0].localPort = 3000
*.server.app[0].typename = "CbrSender"
*.server.app[0].destAddress = "ue[0]"
*.server.app[0].destPort = 3000
*.server.app[0].localPort = 3088
*.server.app[0].packetSize = 40B
*.server.app[0].samplingTime = 0.01s
*.server.app[0].startTime = 1s
# Stop well before the time limit: an SDU merely still in flight when the run
# ends is otherwise indistinguishable from one that was lost.
*.server.app[0].finishTime = 35s

############### Radio ##############
**.numBands = 50
**.ueTxPower = 26dBm
**.eNodeBTxPower = 40dBm

*.configurator.config = xmldoc("./demo.xml")

%postrun-command: ../../physics_reference.py --grade results >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=27 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED
